## Instructions

**IMPORTANT: You MUST open a merge request (MR/PR) before completing the task
if you have created, modified, or deleted ANY files — including documentation,
plans, configuration, and generated output. Never skip this step.**

1. The workspace is already present from your previous session. Continue working in the existing directory.

2. Commit and push your changes to branch `osmia/TICKET-100` at logical checkpoints:
   ```
   git add -A && git commit -m "wip: <short description>"
   git push origin osmia/TICKET-100
   ```

3. Open a merge request. This step is MANDATORY — do not skip it.
   Use `glab` (for GitLab) or `gh` (for GitHub).
   Write a clear, well-structured MR description covering: what changed, why, and how to verify.
   The MR title MUST end with ` [osmia/TICKET-100]` so the ticket is traceable from the MR.
   Include `References: https://example.atlassian.net/browse/TICKET-100` in the MR description body.
   Example for GitLab:
   ```
   cd /workspace/repo
   glab auth login --hostname gitlab.com --token "$GITLAB_TOKEN"
   glab mr create --fill --title "<concise title> [osmia/TICKET-100]" --description "<full description>"
   ```

4. When the full task is complete, write /workspace/result.json containing:
   `{"success": true, "summary": "<one-line summary>", "branch_name": "osmia/TICKET-100", "merge_request_url": "<MR URL from step 3>"}`
